WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Wednesday,

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.680
the twenty-eighth of October.

3
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.320
This episode is written with AI,
and read by an AI clone of my voice.

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.840
Saudi Arabia has contained
a fire near Ras Tanura,

5
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.080
its biggest export terminal, after
a Houthi missile and drone attack,

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.800
and Brent firmed in early Asian trade.

7
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.640
At the same time, Aramco is offering
discounted spot crude to Europe

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.440
from outlets that avoid
the Strait of Hormuz.

9
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.600
On the markets. Brent traded at one
hundred and fifteen dollars seventy

10
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.453
early this morning, up
one point six percent,

11
00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:36.320
according to OilPrice dot com.

12
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.840
West Texas Intermediate was at one
hundred and one dollars twenty,

13
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.760
up one point three percent.

14
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.080
The American Petroleum Institute
estimates US crude stocks fell by about

15
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.480
two million barrels in the week
to the twenty-third of October.

16
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.120
European gas storage stood at
seventy-four point nine percent full on

17
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.720
the twenty-sixth, according
to Gas Infrastructure Europe.

18
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.640
Saudi Arabia said early Tuesday it
intercepted three Houthi ballistic

19
00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.093
missiles aimed at the Eastern Region.

20
00:01:03.147 --> 00:01:06.600
It said it also intercepted
four drones aimed at the south.

21
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.240
A fire then broke out near the Ras
Tanura export hub and was quickly

22
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.040
put out, Bloomberg reported,
citing an unnamed source.

23
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.733
The Houthis say a ballistic missile
hit the Ras Tanura refinery,

24
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:21.013
according to gCaptain.
Riyadh hasn't confirmed that,

25
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:24.520
and no damage to the terminal or
the refinery has been reported.

26
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.440
The site is on the Gulf side.

27
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.240
Any outage would land on loadings
that already depend on Hormuz transits

28
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.213
and ship-to-ship transfers.

29
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:36.000
This morning's gain follows a drop
of nearly two dollars on Tuesday.

30
00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:39.520
Rigzone put that drop down to signs
of de-escalation diplomacy in the

31
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.120
Gulf. Pulling the other way are
reports that Washington is preparing

32
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.240
a new campaign against
Iran after the midterms.

33
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:49.720
Neither the diplomacy nor the
campaign is a confirmed plan;

34
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.640
both rest on reports.

35
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.987
Over to Russia, where crude
is giving way to diesel.

36
00:01:55.093 --> 00:01:58.640
Russian crude exports from Baltic
and Black Sea ports could fall by one

37
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.640
hundred to two hundred thousand
barrels a day in November,

38
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.600
compared with October. That comes from
two traders working from preliminary

39
00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.760
loading schedules, Reuters reported,
and the figures include Kazakh crude

40
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.240
piped through Russia.

41
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.560
The reason is that refiners are running
harder for diesel under the deal

42
00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.200
with Washington struck
on the ninth of October.

43
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.200
That leaves Western buyers
of Urals with fewer barrels,

44
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.560
while more Russian diesel
comes up for export.

45
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.000
Russia's seaborne crude shipments
are already at their lowest in more

46
00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.760
than a month, according to gCaptain,
even though the key Baltic port

47
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.680
has recovered from its halt.

48
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.520
Analysts still expect the diesel
shortage to last into next year,

49
00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.600
OilPrice dot com reports, and they
say the US-Russia deal won't change

50
00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.400
that. Separately, Rigzone reports
that new Indian refining capacity will

51
00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.720
lift diesel exports next year.

52
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.240
Back to Saudi Arabia, and a
change of tone from Aramco.

53
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.000
It is offering European refiners
extra crude for October and November

54
00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.160
loading, Bloomberg reported, citing
a person familiar with the matter.

55
00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.320
Late-October spot cargoes are priced
below the official selling price.

56
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.560
The cargoes load at Yanbu on the
Red Sea, or at Sidi Kerir on Egypt's

57
00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.800
Mediterranean coast. Only weeks ago,
Aramco told customers they'd get

58
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.280
no oil under October contracts after
the East-West pipeline was attacked.

59
00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.440
Shipping from these outlets keeps
the barrels clear of Hormuz.

60
00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.000
European refiners get
medium-sour crude at a discount,

61
00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.840
and other Atlantic Basin sour grades
may find themselves competing harder

62
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.400
for European runs. Aramco is also
close to a ten billion dollar bank

63
00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.320
loan, according to Rigzone.

64
00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.160
In the Strait of Hormuz itself,
Iran's Persian Gulf Strait Authority

65
00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.680
says it will take legal action
against tankers owned by Sinokor,

66
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.867
gCaptain reported. Sinokor is
the world's biggest tanker owner.

67
00:03:43.893 --> 00:03:47.493
It has carried millions of barrels
out of the strait in recent weeks.

68
00:03:47.547 --> 00:03:49.920
For now this is Iran's statement alone.

69
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.640
No action against the
ships has been reported.

70
00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.000
Even so, the backdrop is busier.

71
00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.480
More than thirty incidents have been
recorded in and around Hormuz this

72
00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.920
month, according to OilPrice dot
com, against fourteen in September.

73
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:07.253
The latest target was a crude tanker
in Iraq's exclusive economic zone.

74
00:04:07.307 --> 00:04:10.600
For tanker owners, the view on
Wall Street is getting richer.

75
00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.960
Evercore ISI has doubled its earnings
forecast for very large crude carriers

76
00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.267
next year, from fifty-seven
and a half thousand dollars,

77
00:04:18.373 --> 00:04:20.280
Splash twenty-four seven reported.

78
00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.640
A few more things.

79
00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.120
OPEC plus is expected to leave
December quotas unchanged,

80
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.600
sources told Reuters. Its one point
six five million barrel a day rollback

81
00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:33.520
finished in September, but eight
months of war have made targets largely

82
00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.280
notional, so physical flows
matter more than the decision.

83
00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.560
India's crude basket reached one
hundred and twenty-three dollars thirty

84
00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.160
a barrel last week,
according to local media.

85
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.360
Along with a weak rupee, that has
left fuel marketers losing money even

86
00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.360
after raising pump prices.

87
00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.080
Oil Minister Hardeep Puri denied US
pressure to cut Russian imports and

88
00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.320
said purchases follow price, as Russian
arrivals decline and Middle East

89
00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:03.040
imports rise. Fuel export earnings
reached twenty-seven point two billion

90
00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.880
dollars, according to the oil ministry.

91
00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.520
That covers April to September, and
it is up fifty percent in rupee terms.

92
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.320
On deals, Dangote's refinery share
sale hit its one point six billion

93
00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.040
dollar domestic target,
sources told Bloomberg.

94
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.440
TotalEnergies completed an eight hundred
million dollar sale of its Nigerian

95
00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.560
Renaissance joint venture
interest, World Oil reported.

96
00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.680
Eni is leaving Nigeria's onshore upstream,

97
00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:31.680
according to Rigzone. And Woodside
is selling its Greater Sunrise stake

98
00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.600
for up to two hundred million dollars.

99
00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.840
US offshore regulators' shut-in
figures for Hurricane Isaias are still

100
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.640
pending. They were due on
the sixteenth of October.

101
00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.440
What to watch next. Today, the EIA's
weekly figures for the week to the

102
00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:49.200
twenty-third of October. On
Sunday, the first of November,

103
00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.760
OPEC plus meets on December quotas.

104
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.200
Monday brings a Russian
diesel tanker due in Norfolk.

105
00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.480
And on Tuesday, the third,
come the US midterms,

106
00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.320
the date the reports tie to
a possible new Iran campaign.

107
00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.000
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
